From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-eip: remove unused invalidation device pointer

The synchronous transform-record invalidation changes left an eip_pdev
pointer in eip_tr_inval_done() after its last user was removed.  Drop the
dead declaration and assignment so the driver builds cleanly with W=1.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/tree/10a89a95f814cd325e23105f102428644f45014f
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
--- a/driver/eip197/eip_tr.c
+++ b/driver/eip197/eip_tr.c
@@ -88,11 +88,9 @@ static void eip_tr_dummy_err(void *app_d
  */
 static void eip_tr_inval_done(struct eip_tr *tr, struct eip_hw_desc *hw, struct eip_sw_desc *sw)
 {
-	struct eip_pdev *ep;
 	struct eip_ctx *ctx;
 
 	ctx = tr->ctx;
-	ep = ctx->ep;
 
 	/*
 	 * free the memory associated with the operation.
